\f1\b0  In highly competitive environments, your high humility might be misinterpreted as a lack of confidence, while your strategic pragmatism (if kept hidden) might occasionally surprise colleagues who only expect your empathetic side.\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 2. Top 3 Behavioral Risks\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Masking Competence:
\f1\b0  Because your humility is exceptionally high, you may habitually deflect praise or underplay your expertise. This can inadvertently undermine your authority or cause senior stakeholders to underestimate your team's impact.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Strategic Withholding:
\f1\b0  Your moderate Machiavellianism means you are naturally skilled at reading a room and calculating the best path forward. If you map out strategies internally without bringing others along on the journey, colleagues may feel excluded or distrustful of your methods.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Over-Indexing on Consensus:
\f1\b0  Your empathy and humility might drive you to seek universal agreement, which can slow down critical decision-making in crisis scenarios.\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\li4620\fi-4620\ri4620\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 3. Top 3 Protective Strengths\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
