\f1\b0  You create deep psychological safety. Because you aren't fighting for the spotlight, your team feels valued and heard, offsetting the risk of them feeling managed or manipulated.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Moral Anchoring (Ethical Leadership 79):
\f1\b0  This is your strongest regulatory mechanism. It ensures that your strategic instincts (Machiavellianism) are always deployed for the greater good of the organization rather than personal gain.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Measured Reactivity (Low Psychopathy 39 / Sadism 43):
\f1\b0  You are unlikely to lead through fear or lash out under pressure. This emotional stability builds long-term trust and offsets any friction that arises from difficult operational decisions.\uc0\u8232 \
